  "asr_text": "If you become more serious, will you earn more? Or do you become more serious once you start earning more? When you hear about research on income and personality, you might expect to learn the secret of high earners, but this time the people in the spotlight are not some rich people. They are your former self and your later self. The research brought together 11 large studies. They looked at people who were working and had reported on their personality and income from work. The number of people varied by analysis, but the researchers used data from as many as 134,515 people. In every study, the same people's income and personality were measured at least three times. The key was how the researchers compared people. They analyzed separately the differences between people that tend not to change and changes that happen within each person.",
